  "summary_en": "China's State Council General Office issues the 14th Five-Year National Health Plan (2022), setting public health, healthcare, TCM, and health industry goals to 2025/2035. Only passing provisions touch AI and robotics: promoting AI medical equipment, intelligent service robots, rehabilitation assistive devices, and AI in smart healthcare.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Targets for 2025 include life expectancy up about one year and a stronger public health system.",
   "Promotes high-quality medical equipment integrating AI and moves qualifying AI products into clinical trials.",
   "Advances intelligent service robots and rehabilitation assistive devices for smart ageing.",
   "Applies AI, big data, 5G and IoT to smart medical services and disease early warning.",
   "Requires strict management of citizen health information and data security across its lifecycle."
